# DIAGNOSTICS

Every call returns `VX_ERR_BAD_HANDLE` for a handle that is not open or not a task, and `VX_ERR_ACCESS` for one without the right it needs.

`vx_task_create` and `vx_task_fork` return:

: `VX_OK`
  The handle is in <out>.
: `VX_ERR_RANGE`
  <name> is 24 bytes or longer.
: `VX_ERR_INVALID`
  <name> or <out> is not mapped in the caller, or an option other than `VX_TASK_FORK` was given.
: `VX_ERR_NO_MEMORY`
  The kernel has no room for the task or, for a fork, for the copy.
: `VX_ERR_BAD_STATE`
  A fork's caller is being torn down.

`vx_task_exec` returns only on a failure, having changed nothing:

: `VX_ERR_INVALID`
  <entry> or <sp> is outside user space, <scratch> is the caller, or <bootstrap> is the caller or <scratch>.
: `VX_ERR_BAD_STATE`
  The caller has another live thread or is ending, or <scratch> has started, ended, or is another exec's.
: `VX_ERR_BAD_HANDLE`, `VX_ERR_ACCESS`
  Also for a <bootstrap> that is not open, or lacks `VX_RIGHT_TRANSFER`.
: `VX_ERR_NO_MEMORY`
  No room for the new thread.

If the new program's thread cannot then be started, the task ends with the exit string `exec failed`.

`vx_task_info` and `vx_task_info_of` return `VX_OK`; `VX_ERR_NOT_FOUND` when there is no task <id> in the tree, or none after it; `VX_ERR_INVALID` for a flag other than `VX_TASK_NEXT`, or an <out> not mapped writable.

`vx_task_kill` and `vx_task_kill_id` return `VX_OK`; `VX_ERR_RANGE` for a <msg> longer than `VX_ERRMAX`; `VX_ERR_INVALID` when <msg> is not mapped; `VX_ERR_NOT_FOUND` as above.

`vx_task_mem_rw` returns `VX_OK`, or `VX_ERR_INVALID` for a <count> of 0 or more than 16, or <ops> not mapped writable.
An operation's <status> is:

: `VX_OK`
  All of it was copied.
: `VX_ERR_RANGE`
  It is longer than 1 MiB, or runs past the end of user space.
: `VX_ERR_INVALID`
  Part of it is mapped in neither the task nor, for <buffer>, the caller.
: `VX_ERR_UNSUPPORTED`
  It touches device memory, or writes to pages a pager supplies.
: `VX_ERR_SHOULD_WAIT`
  It reads a pager's page that has not been supplied.
: `VX_ERR_NO_MEMORY`
  No room for a private copy, or more than 16 mappings needed one in this call; the caller may try again.

# BUGS

An operation of `vx_task_mem_rw` that fails part way has copied the pages before the failure, and its <status> does not say how many bytes.

A private copy made for a write is of the whole mapping, made at once; the mapping no longer sees later changes to the VMO it came from.

A fork copies every page at once: pages shared until written, behind the same call, are later work.

`vx_task_exec` starts the new program's thread after the old address space has gone, so a failure there can only end the task.
